{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_handoff_gap_handoff_gap_tsv", "label": "HANDOFF-GAP.tsv \u2014 the handoffs the corpus names and holds nowhere", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "88 cited by bare number, 62 held before the recovery, 23 seated by it, 3 still held nowhere. The provenance record carries byte length, line count, md5, the message that holds each one and seated_as."}, {"id": "docs_handoff_gap_recovered_by_number", "label": "RECOVERED-BY-NUMBER is its own status", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "These were reachable only through a bare-number citation and never through the wanted-set; flattening them to RECOVERED would lose exactly the fact that made them findable."}, {"id": "docs_handoff_gap_wanted_set_shape", "label": "The wanted-set's shape, not the tool's idempotence", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Twenty-five of the twenty-six are never written in filename shape, so they were never wanted; COVERAGE.tsv is byte-identical after seating, which is the confirmation rather than a surprise."}, {"id": "docs_handoff_gap_structural_read", "label": "Read the export structurally, not as text", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A handoff's body is a tool call's file_text, so a prose-only extractor reports all 26 as mentions and a regex pass reports 15 where the true figure is 23."}, {"id": "docs_handoff_gap_mention_only", "label": "MENTION-ONLY is not a finding of loss", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HANDOFF-2, 103 and 104: the name is spoken and no body exists in the export, which is the conservative call rather than an absence."}, {"id": "docs_handoff_gap_nested_json_trap", "label": "The export nests JSON inside JSON", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Newlines arrive double-escaped, so a ^-anchored heading pattern matches nothing; and an unanchored cat matches the middle of truncated, which is how a pass claimed a written body from the phrase truncated middle of HANDOFF-54."}, {"id": "docs_handoff_gap_generator_excludes_own", "label": "The generator excludes its own recoveries from the held-test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Otherwise the file erases its own history on the first regeneration: the 23 are seated, a naive held-test drops them, and the record of where they came from goes too."}], "edges": [{"source": "claude_status_never_flattened", "target": "docs_handoff_gap_recovered_by_number", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_coverage_floor_not_total", "target": "docs_handoff_gap_handoff_gap_tsv", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_handoff_gap_handoff_gap_tsv", "target": "docs_graph_findings_two_numberings", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/HANDOFF-GAP.md", "source_loc